# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Wired by 1087-h2z9.
#
# Triaged from scripts/gate-divergence-declared.txt, where it sat `untriaged`
# since 2026-09-06: present in --ci-full, absent from --check, nobody decided.
# Measured green and cheap on b026372ff (Guard activation audit), so the honest verdict is to run
# it where every host lands rather than once a day on the release gate.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf): a binding assembled
# from a variable is invisible to every name-based scan. Ported from
# audit-guard-activation.sh by 1570-25iq; the verdict line is now house-
# prefixed (ok:/violation:guard-activation:population=...).
STEP_DESC="Auditing that every guard is actually wired"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/audit-guard-activation.lua"
STEP_ERROR="a guard exists but nothing invokes it (1087-h2z9)"
STEP_OK="Guard activation audit passed"
# The second-regime record below was taken on the .sh. The port (1570-25iq)
# has not yet been run on darwin or msys; it is pure fs reads with no spawn,
# no symlink-following and no grep, which removes the regime differences the
# .sh had (1087-h2z9), but that is an argument, not a measurement.
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:rc0-no-verdict-line"
